  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Retain zero-distance cancellation stress with bounded branch alternatives while preserving native solver arithmetic and strict output tolerances.",
  "regressions": [
    "All 17 original boundary configurations remain mandatory, including tail sizes, bias/friction modes, seeds and up to three passes.",
    "Generate counterfactual alternatives from the current Rust solver source; its unforced result must match original Rust output bit for bit.",
    "Independently recompute f32 roundoff intervals in Rust and Python and reject invented ambiguity, excessive interval width, multiple ambiguous points and nonfinite transforms.",
    "Require all impulses and both body velocities of a manifold to match one complete native soft/hard outcome; reject component mixtures, invented nonambiguous outcomes, modified readonly buffers and guards.",
    "Hash both scene and boundary numerical policy documents in the conservative implementation envelope."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "No Rust or TileLang physics arithmetic is changed. The original atol 2e-6 and rtol 2e-5 remain.",
    "This explicitly accepts different CFM branches only when bounded f32 rounding can change the sign; it is not bitwise parity and does not excuse unrelated mismatches.",
    "Native Rust Metal diagnostic residuals in nonambiguous cases remain separate diagnostic evidence; only registered target reports establish execution parity.",
    "Ascend vendor compilation, execution and synchronization remain unvalidated."
  ],
  "related_changes": [
    "0058-contact-sensitive-scene-numerics"
  ]
}
